les of some beautiful  unused concept art of alkali lake by  designer shake shack and there was  another idea for a flashback scene  featuring the location where the movie  villains lived a residence which  included a pool a helipad and a killer  view the unused concept art also reveals  an alternate design for the tank where  Charles was being kept by Logan and  curiously in some early sketches  it looks like Logan originally had a  little canine companion which might have  given him more of a Mad Max vibe and it  was an Oklahoma City where we might have  seen a reunion between Logan and Victor  Creed aka Sabretooth as the Logan movie  was being developed  Liev Schreiber expressed interest in  reprising the role of Sabretooth one  final time and an early idea was mooted  that Logan would seek out his  half-brother and former nemesis  Sabretooth for help it was never to be  though and the IDF fell by the wayside  but would you have liked to seen the  pair back together before Hugh Jackman's  retirement as Wolverine I gotta say I  love the tone they went for in the final  movie and various mutant cameos might  not have fit so well with that purr down  story still although the Wolverine clone  x24 was played by Hugh Jackman himself  if you get a smite sabre to survive when  x24 first appeared during that brutal  fight scene at the Munson family home  the dinner conversation that Logan and  Charles have with the Munson's could  have been much darker as an alternate  versions of scene with films where the  Munson's asked Logan if he's married  Charles replies that Logan was married  but that he killed her man Gould  explained that he didn't use that  version of the scene because it felt  just too dark at the moment in the film  that was meant to provide a little  levity especially with the events which  happened later at the Munson farm by the  way if that scene had made it into the  final film it's unclear what exactly  that would have meant to the x-men  timeline which after Days of Future past  appeared to invalidate the timeline of  the first three x-men movies at the end  of which Wolverine killed Jean Grey  early in the story director James  Mangold also toyed with the idea of  Logan reaching a group of other mutants  on an underground railroad during his  journey the mutants would probably have  been cameos by characters at Suns would  recognize however Mangold decided at  including them would have felt forced  given the movie's tone and ultimately  they would have undermined a loneliness  of Logan's world one character that fans  have been desperate to see alongside  Wolverine and for a long time was  rumored to appear in Logan it's Deadpool  it would have been great to see  Wolverine and Deadpool on-screen  together you know in a good film not  just x-men origins Wolverine but as Ryan  Reynolds explained the Merc with a mouth  wouldn't have mixed with the tone of  Logan Wade Wilson and Deadpool did get a  little teaser for Deadpool to complete  with a cameo by Stan Lee in the short no  good deed but the way that the movie  Logan worked out in terms of mood and  storyline for me it was better that  Deadpool wasn't part of the main film  the supervillain mr. sinister aka  Nathaniel Essex was teased in the x-men  apocalypse  post-credits with brian fingers taking  the third Wolverine movie would  introduce the villain properly however  later james mangold decided not to  include the flashy supervillain in Logan  and he wanted to keep the film very  grounded and step away from the huge  spectacle of the other movies and the  x-men franchise man goals wanted the  audience to feel as if they could run  into Wolverine on the street so he made  the choice to avoid including  larger-than-life villains in brightly  colored costumes like mr. sinister but  don't despair if you are a fan of the  mr. sinister character as Simon Kinberg  has now said that mr. sinister will be  introduced in a future x-men movie it  was certainly a great